  "verbalization": "Lippiolidolic acid appears to interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C through a multi-step pathway, with SNU-387 acting as a common intermediate in multiple connections. The evidence suggests that Lippiolidolic acid targets SNU-387, which is a target of several compounds, including Fluostatin I, 5-Hydroxytryptophan monohydrate, and Eryngiolide A. All these compounds ultimately have a target of Phosphodiesterase 6C. This implies that Lippiolidolic acid may exert its effects through a shared mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of SNU-387, which in turn influences Phosphodiesterase 6C. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Phosphodiesterase 6C suggests a potential role in downstream physiological processes, though the exact mechanism of interaction between Lippiolidolic acid and SNU-387 remains to be elucidated. The integration of these findings highlights the importance of SNU-387 as a central node in the network of targets, reinforcing the likelihood of a functional link between Lippiolidolic acid and Phosphodiesterase 6C.",
